WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.751
Partitions are central to Spark parallelism A
dataset is divided

00:00:05.777 --> 00:00:11.346
into pieces and tasks process those pieces Too few
partitions

00:00:11.373 --> 00:00:18.451
can limit parallelism Too many small partitions can
create overhead As

00:00:18.478 --> 00:00:22.741
a beginner you do not need to tune every partition
setting but you should understand

00:00:22.767 --> 00:00:24.688
why partitioning affects performance
